WHY THIS IS VENDORED

ARC's real proving path is feature-gated behind `stwo-prover`. While Stwo was
tracked as a git dependency, two things were outside our control:

  1. Upstream uses nightly-only APIs. `array_chunks_mut` was removed from later
     nightlies, which broke the build entirely — and because the feature is
     optional, the failure mode was a silent fall back to the BLAKE3 mock path
     rather than a hard error. rust-toolchain.toml pins around it; vendoring
     removes the dependency on that pin holding.

  2. The prover internals were not ours to change. The GPU backend work needs
     to modify them.

MODIFICATIONS FROM UPSTREAM

  * The `examples` crate is not vendored (not used by ARC).
  * Cargo.toml is a workspace root over the vendored crates rather than
    `crates/*`; the ARC root workspace excludes this directory.

Source changes, all confined to stwo/src/ and all mechanical API migrations
required to build on Rust nightlies newer than 2025-06-01:

  * `<[T]>::array_chunks` / `array_chunks_mut` were renamed to `as_chunks` /
    `as_chunks_mut`, and now return `(&[[T; N]], &[T])` rather than an
    iterator. Call sites updated to `.as_chunks::<N>().0.iter()`.
      prover/backend/cpu/circle.rs
      prover/backend/cpu/fri.rs
      prover/backend/simd/circle.rs
      prover/backend/simd/column.rs
      prover/backend/simd/prefix_sum.rs
      prover/backend/simd/lookups/gkr.rs
      prover/backend/cpu/lookups/gkr.rs

    `Iterator::array_chunks` (feature `iter_array_chunks`) is a different
    method and still exists; those call sites are unchanged.

  * `ArrayChunks::into_remainder` now returns the remainder directly instead
    of `Option<_>`. Three sites in prover/backend/simd/column.rs updated.

  * The `array_chunks` feature gate was dropped from stwo/src/lib.rs, as the
    slice methods are no longer behind it. `portable_simd`, `slice_ptr_get`
    and `iter_array_chunks` are still required, so a nightly toolchain is
    still needed — just not a nine-month-old one.

VERIFICATION

The migration was checked for behavioural equivalence, not just compilation.
`examples/receipt_probe.rs` proves fixed layers through both the packed and
unpacked AIRs and prints the full proof receipts. Receipts from the patched
vendored copy on nightly-2026-03-16 are byte-identical to those from
unmodified upstream on nightly-2025-06-01, across both circuits and both
layer sizes. Stwo's own test suite passes, including the FRI negative tests
that check invalid proofs are rejected.

Re-run the comparison after any future upstream sync:

    cargo run --release -p arc-crypto --features stwo-prover --example receipt_probe

